{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JtcFZ13qrCiHZzevV4BQbZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Cloning into 'engine-src'...\nAI_GUIDE.md\nAPI-INDEX.md\nAPI.md\nREADME.md\ndocs\ngame\nindex.html\nkits\nmodules\nmy-3d2dge-agent.js\nmy-3d2dge.js\npackage.json\nsrc\ntools\n4.9M\tdist/handoff\ntmpfs           9.8G  9.7G   66M 100% /tmp\n/dev/sdd       1007G  133G  824G  14% /","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eb1a01c-ab9c-4627-8921-fbc800f925bb","uuid":"fc5faddf-5486-4cc5-8f7a-df03ef0c6c96","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:03.685Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Cloning into 'engine-src'...\nAI_GUIDE.md\nAPI-INDEX.md\nAPI.md\nREADME.md\ndocs\ngame\nindex.html\nkits\nmodules\nmy-3d2dge-agent.js\nmy-3d2dge.js\npackage.json\nsrc\ntools\n4.9M\tdist/handoff\ntmpfs           9.8G  9.7G   66M 100% /tmp\n/dev/sdd       1007G  133G  824G  14% /","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":181,"oldLines":3,"newStart":181,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Bibn99tLypPy2mGw9AGiQ2\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\\n- `arcade.o`: the options\\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\\n\\n## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"2fc1d37e-51a1-40f5-a9ad-e7e2f4ac28a1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:57.050Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\\n- `arcade.o`: the options\\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\\n\\n## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\",\"stderr\":\"\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Bibn99tLypPy2mGw9AGiQ2\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"b91adf75-7cf7-4079-9315-1f33ef1fd28a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"fece74a8-2fd7-429a-851c-571e9b5c8399\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":450,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"d301f794-be81-4fcb-b2b3-8ededa125b5e\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"9f6fe4ea-5529-4d63-9621-99a6cdcc6c8d\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"48e437be-92fa-45e7-82fa-7b0da4cb71d7\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183606__xf7f297/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":81,"oldLines":3,"newStart":81,"newLines":7,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"a4a44736-05d8-46ca-bbc2-d0beaa732c41\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":471,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":171,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"5856eaec-f3fc-40c4-96b7-8c7d7f43266f\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2mxR6PzX8rASZcA6EA\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6185,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":89413,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6185},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"6ab3d46d-4237-428d-8d55-cbb482de7840\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:59.259Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2mxADXBLkWt72982x5\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":2620,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2mxR6PzX8rASZcA6EA\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I have the mission pattern. Now I need the Shell (HTML UI) and sight/cut APIs before writing code, so I'll grep the API for them.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6185,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":89413,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6185},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"79b884c7-74ac-40ec-9c3c-3706e28bf4bb\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:59.582Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2mxADXBLkWt72982x5\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2mxR6PzX8rASZcA6EA\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01KoupjZv9tYGvy4FwRofPZ3\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n 'Shell\\\\|sightCone\\\\|marker\\\\|E.sees\\\\|Suspicion\\\\|Attack\\\\b\\\\|E.Menu\\\\|hits(\\\\|inArc\\\\|knockback\\\\|sameLevel\\\\|E.Mover\\\\|rigState\\\\|rollAt\\\\|E.Dialog\\\\|talk' API.md | cut -c1-300 | head -60; echo ----; grep -n 'Shell\\\\.\\\\(show\\\\|hud\\\\|toast\\\\|hide\\\\|page\\\\|menu\\\\)\\\\|class Shell\\\\|E.Shell\\\\|_hud\\\\|show(name\\\\|hud(' API-INDEX.md | head -30\",\"description\":\"Grep API for Shell, sight, mover and menu APIs\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6185,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":89413,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6185},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"d9c8371c-131e-4acb-ba6b-a36bfb6091d2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:37:01.051Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2mxADXBLkWt72982x5\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01KoupjZv9tYGvy4FwRofPZ3\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183606__xf7f297/work/dev && grep -n 'Shell\\\\|sightCone\\\\|marker\\\\|E.sees\\\\|Suspicion\\\\|Attack\\\\b\\\\|E.Menu\\\\|hits(\\\\|inArc\\\\|knockback\\\\|sameLevel\\\\|E.Mover\\\\|rigState\\\\|rollAt\\\\|E.Dialog\\\\|talk' API.md | cut -c1-300 | head -60; echo ----; grep -n 'Shell\\\\.\\\\(show\\\\|hud\\\\|toast\\\\|hide\\\\|page\\\\|menu\\\\)\\\\|class Shell\\\\|E.Shell\\\\|_hud\\\\|show(name\\\\|hud(' API-INDEX.md | head -30\",\"description\":\"Grep API for Shell, sight, mover and menu APIs\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01KoupjZv9tYGvy4FwRofPZ3\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183606__xf7f297/work/dev\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01KoupjZv9tYGvy4FwRofPZ3\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"7:**Looking a name up:** grep `API-INDEX.md` (every public name, one line; members are filed under instance names: `rig.`, `talk.`, `mover.`, `flow.`, `map.`), not the engine's source. It, the guide (`AI_GUIDE.md`) and the tools are in the handoff package (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/handoff/) and the repo\\n51:10. **Faces in dialog**: `talk.say(lines, { name: 'MIRA', portrait: miraRig })` puts a live close-up of that Humanoid (blinking, hair, hat) beside every line. `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40)` draws one anywhere (HUD, RPG party windows).\\n58:| `'iso'` (yaw 45, pitch 30) | Diablo, Landstalker | x/y ground, z up | `E.TileMap` | `E.Body` |\\n76:7. Put the whole game in one IIFE `(() => { ... })();` between the markers, and start it with `game.start(...)`.\\n144:- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch buttons cover the screen (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }` in screen pixels, or null): keep a prompt clear of \\n160:- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while \\n161:- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel })`; `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse o\\n162:- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme, settings, screens: { pause, help } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(t\\n176:**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `e\\n185:- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\\n187:- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (i\\n190:**Body** (top-down / isometric / brawler): `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, friction: 0, bounce: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Set `vx`, `vy`, then `body.update(dt, map)`. Also `push(ix, iy, iz)` (knockback), `jump(v)`, and `onGround`, `z`, `groundZ`, `hitWall`, `landed`, `bounced` (hit the ground and bounced: \\n192:**Mover** (third person): `const mover = new E.Mover({ x, y })`; `mover.update(dt, map, game.input)` (input `'THIRDPERSON'`) or an AI's `{ move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }`: it sprints, sneaks, climbs, vaults, leaps gaps, hops down and rolls; `climbAny: true` climbs any wall (jump a\\n194:**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover }`. `if (input.buffered('attack') && slash.start()) in\\n198:**Helpers**: `E.dist(a, b)`, `E.angleTo(a, b)`, `E.arc(a, b, gravity, { apex | time | speed })` → `{ vx, vy, vz, t }` (a throw that lands at b: a lob, a grenade), `E.overlap(a, b)` (circles x, y, r), `E.overlapBox(a, b)` (side boxes x center, z feet, w, h), `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngl\\n212:- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (victory with the weapon raised, spell casting, a boxer's guard, hurt or resting, ducking, greeting, a cocky idle, knocked out; they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon held upri\\n227:| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\\n228:| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, p\\n230:| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\\n231:| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\\n232:| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\\n242:| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's build order and waves; `cam.free`, `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick`, buildings as `E.SHAPES`, E.Shell\\n249:| Third-person stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu) | `iso` / `threequarter` | TileMap roofs, Mover, `E.sees`, `E.Suspicion`, FlowField `jump` | STEALTH |\\n271:  - `rooms`: a world of rooms on a grid of screens (`E.World`): walking between them at open edges (a slide or a fade, the camera's bounds), the explored map (`drawMap`, or `shellMap()` for `E.Shell`), gates that abilities or keys open, saves in `E.store`. METROIDVANIA.\\n275:  - `story`: dialogue as data (`E.Story`): nodes of lines with speakers and portraits, choices with conditions, flags and values (`{$name}` in lines), gotos, the game's events (one may hold the talk), a quest log, emote balloons over heads, a backlog, auto and skip; its state for a save. RPG, PO\\n278:  - `click` (the full engine only): point-and-click adventures (`E.Click`): rooms painted once, walk areas with holes (`E.Walkbox`: the shortest way round), depth scale, hotspots (rectangles, polygons, actors) with verbs, a place to stand and a way to face, SCUMM's nine verbs, Sierra's icons, a \\n287:- One IIFE starting with `const E = My3D2dge` (between the markers in a single file; `game/game.js` in the handoff package). Only your game: no leftover starter menu or unused slices. No network, no libraries.\\n289:- The camera follows the player (`game.focus` every update) and shows the level; the HUD uses screen pixels, or `E.Shell`'s HTML for a modern game (the STEALTH kit; the handoff package's template).\\n293:- Animation variety: every character has its own moves from `E.MOVES` (not one shared swing), enemies telegraph with a visible wind-up, and reactions play out (hurt, knockback, `down`, victory `cheer`).\\n----\\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\\n1172:- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\\n1173:- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\\n1174:- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\\n1175:- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\\n1176:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\\n1177:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\\n1178:- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\\n1181:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\\n1326:- `race.hud(r, R, o = {})`: the standard HUD for a racer, in its viewport: place, lap, time, item, the countdown, WRONG WAY, FINISH (o.color; o.right: the x its right-hand text ends before, clear of a corner button)\\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"332c1f02-8f02-4356-814b-807307d9a6dc\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:37:01.0