in, effect, skill, class, monster, knight, item, castle, map, site, event,","   realm, song, voice`. A validation suite checks that every id a spec refers to exists. Content never edits the code","-  that runs it.","+  that runs it. This is how the rest of the game gets built later with ordinary designer tools: tables, ASCII maps and","+  story nodes that a designer edits and the `data` suite checks, plus dev mode's jump, trigger and gallery tools to try","+  any piece in seconds."," - **Simulations.** `G.BattleSim` and `G.CampaignSim` keep their state as plain JSON. They never touch the engine, the","   DOM, the clock or `Math.random`. Each one offers `legal(...)`, `apply(cmd) → events[]`, `forecast(...)` (battle),","   `serialize()`, `G.*Sim.load(json)` and `hash()`. Randomness comes from `G.Rng` (mulberry32), whose state lives inside"]},{"oldStart":1521,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1523,"newLines":9,"lines":[" Battle ambient light by season: Spring .8 (cool green), Summer .95 (warm), Autumn .7 (amber), Winter .65 (blue). The"," Hour places are dark (.45): brass lamps and the clock's glow light them."," ","+TASK.md treats the performance budget as unlimited, and FPS targets and optimization are out of scope. Add the detail,","+lights, shadows, weather and effects each scene needs, and spend no time on frame-rate work.","+"," ### 7.2 The battlefield (`31-art-hexfield.js`)"," - **The floor** is a wall-less `E.TileMap({ w, h, floorTex, outside })` sized to the field plus 2 tiles of margin.","   - `floorTex(x, y)` finds the hex with `G.hex.toCell` (cube rounding, not a search) and colours it with that terrain's"]},{"oldStart":1979,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1984,"newLines":9,"lines":["   5. warm the first beast portraits.","   Boot messages: \"Winding the Great Clock\", \"Teaching wyverns to sit\", \"Counting the bells\", \"Sweeping the cross-quarter","   roads\".","-- **The title** (§8.5.1) tracks idle time: any key, mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or","-  touch resets it. At 10 s it goes to `attract`.","+- **The title** (§8.5.1) and the setup menus before play (campaign setup, skirmish setup) track idle time: any key,","+  mouse button, pointer move over 4 px, pad button, stick past .5 or touch resets it. At 10 s they go to `attract`.","+  Reading screens (About, How to Play) and anything in play never do."," - **On a touch-only device** (coarse pointer, no fine pointer, touch points, no gamepad or keyboard seen): show the","   \"Controller or keyboard required\" panel with a large Settings button (`game.menu('settings')`) and no touch controls","   (`touch: []` in every scene, `input.touchEnabled = false`). The idle timer still runs. A gamepad connecting or a key"]},{"oldStart":2247,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2253,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - The Node harness loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine-ext/beasts.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the","   stand-ins `kits/test.mjs` uses (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). It drives the game with `game.advance`,","   `input.tap` / `hold` / `feed` and `game.debug`.","+- As TASK.md asks: test with headless tools and scripts that play the game and read its state; take screenshots only","+  for what a script can't check (§14.4); rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (§14.7); and don't use","+  subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit."," "," ### 14.2 Suites (each line names what it proves)"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":520,"oldLines":3,"newStart":520,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610\",\"uuid\":\"65eedb29-f928-4302-84bc-240c41b51dca\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":