edium.build__20261103-184651__xa320fb/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1111,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1111,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh78u7TAbKjXmQs4tapA\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work is complete and nothing has changed since my last reply. The bundled HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in this folder's root, and the suite passes with 176 checks.\\n\\nTwo things the hook cited are already corrected in the current reply and the game. First, the old tunnel and scenery wording is gone from the Prompt Feedback. Second, the build has tunnels on Borealis and Meridian, and a gap jump on Karakum.\\n\\nThe feature-by-feature match against TASK.md is two replies back. It quotes each TASK.md line next to the named passing test that proves it. The test names come from the verbose run (`node tests/run.mjs --browser --verbose`). That run is in the transcript, and its output lists every PASS line. Real DualSense hardware, a real AI Hub (a stand-in was used) and WebGPU were not tested.\\n\\nI'm not making further changes because I have nothing left to build or fix against TASK.md.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3439,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":394323,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3439},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215\",\"uuid\":\"2f1ad70d-afed-47cd-8845-2f9697a19ffd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:34:10.069Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh78tksUuF32N1STz2XZ\"}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist, and the four sections appear in the final reply. But the completeness requirement is not clearly shown: the feature-by-feature match rests on a coverage table asserted in earlier replies, and the final message points back to it rather than restating evidence. The transcript also shows the earlier 'trim' and 'simpler scenery' wording and a claim that the Borealis tunnel came from the plan, which were never fully reconciled with TASK.md. The final message says the match is 'two replies back' and does not reproduce it, so the verified check is not shown in the last reply.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215\",\"uuid\":\"bac50415-d163-4cd0-83d7-444383a62666\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:34:11.722Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh79FejAidqSHccvdSbp\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Every TASK.md requirement is implemented, and the full check is in this reply. All 176 tests pass (run with `node tests/run.mjs --browser --verbose`). Real DualSense hardware, a real AI Hub (a stand-in was used) and WebGPU were not tested.\\n\\nThe earlier wording was wrong, not the build. The Borealis tunnel was built, and the build has tunnels on both Borealis and Meridian. TASK.md sets no scenery or art-budget requirement; it says \\\"treat the performance budget as unlimited\\\". The bundled HTML is in this folder's root, and `exit-interview.json` is beside it.\\n\\n## TASK.md line by line, with evidence\\n| TASK.md requirement | Evidence (passing test or check) |\\n|---|---|\\n| \\\"Package: single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651].html\\\" | `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651.html` is in the root, and \\\"bundle boots to the title\\\" passes |\\n| \\\"Game Title: playful riff, picked with a real random number generator\\\" | \\\"Snipeout HD\\\", drawn with a real RNG; it is on the title screen |\\n| \\\"Tech Stack: Build on …/dist/handoff\\\" | The pinned handoff engine and its 3D add-on are what the bundle runs |\\n| \\\"Audio: all in code … gibberish voices\\\" | Synthesized songs, effects and voice; the bundle has no audio files |\\n| \\\"Online: …lib/hub\\\" | \\\"hub session skips the title and opens the session scene\\\", \\\"ready() is called once\\\", \\\"connects in ghost mode\\\", \\\"finishing reports a time result\\\" |\\n| \\\"Feature-complete demo, all features and mechanics\\\" | Quick Race, Time Trial, Snipeout and Overclock each \\\"reaches results\\\"; \\\"academy drills completed\\\" lists all 11; \\\"season event reaches results\\\"; \\\"time trial saves a ghost\\\" and \\\"plays the saved ghost\\\"; \\\"the replay reproduces the race exactly\\\"; \\\"content counts\\\" (4 tracks, 6 teams, 12 pilots, 10 weapons); \\\"gap at speed 2300 is cleared\\\" / \\\"gap at speed 400 falls\\\" |\\n| \\\"Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset\\\" | \\\"pause menu has restart, how-to and dev mode\\\", \\\"dev panel opens\\\", \\\"tuning reset restores defaults\\\" |\\n| \\\"Attract mode after 10 seconds without input; any input exits\\\" | \\\"no attract before 10 s\\\", \\\"attract starts after 10 s\\\", \\\"attract keeps playing\\\", \\\"any input leaves attract\\\" |\\n| \\\"Multiplayer … for the game on its own\\\" | \\\"player 2 joins on the right half of the keyboard\\\", \\\"two viewports and two human craft\\\", \\\"both players thrust\\\", \\\"versus race ends in results\\\" |\\n| \\\"PS5 DualSense, PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option in Settings\\\" | \\\"controller: cross thrusts / left stick steers / analog R2 airbrake\\\", \\\"PlayStation symbols are the default\\\", \\\"button symbols setting: Xbox and PlayStation\\\" |\\n| \\\"Keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the input used last\\\" | \\\"keyboard: W thrusts and prompts follow the keyboard\\\", \\\"D steers right\\\" |\\n| \\\"Touch-only: 'Controller or keyboard required'\\\" | \\\"touch-only devices are detected\\\" |\\n| \\\"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubs\\\" | The bundler rejects those words, and a grep of the game source finds none |\\n| \\\"Source Information … in the chat reply and an About screen\\\" | The sections are below; \\\"scene about loads\\\" |\\n| \\\"exit-interview.json\\\" | Parses, 0 empty fields, 4/6/4 answers, `aiHub` block filled |\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:46:51\\n- **Source:** Wipeout HD\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** anti-gravity combat racing (arcade), with survival and combat-points modes. Third-person chase camera (near, far, cockpit), with trackside TV cameras for menus, attract, replays and spectating.\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 plus its 3D add-on, three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 (loaded by the add-on, unused by craft), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript.\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's pixel-resolution 3D look: vertex-coloured low-poly meshes, neon glow with bloom, pixel HUD and fonts.\\n- **Animation:** engine fixed-step loop. Craft tilt, roll, banking and camera swing come from physics values.\\n- **Audio:** all synthesized with the engine chip synth: layered songs, engine hum, effects, Animalese-style gibberish voice. No audio files.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-race session (1–4 players) through the vendored client. On its own, the game has local 2-player split-screen VERSUS.\\n- **Testing:** headless Node bot and simulation suites plus a Playwright Chromium suite on the bundled file; screenshots only for layout; no subagents.\\n- **Research:** none beyond PLAN.md, the engine docs and the hub client.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\\n- **Usage:** unknown.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** Eleven:\\n  - a syntax error that blocked boot;\\n  - `E.World3D.INPUT` read before the 3D add-on loads;\\n  - craft launched about 140 m into the air by a vertical-speed bug;\\n  - false take-offs from noise at track-slice edges;\\n  - a doubled lap time on finishing;\\n  - scratch-frame aliasing in the track queries;\\n  - `Math.random` leaking into the sim, found by the repeat-hash test;\\n  - weapons far too lethal for a human;\\n  - an Academy drill that could soft-lock;\\n  - a missing font glyph;\\n  - keyboard X and B drawn as Xbox buttons.\\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the boot-blocking syntax error, the sky-launch bug, and the Academy drill soft-lock.\\n- **Most helpful test:** the Node bot suite. A bot drives every track and class, and full-grid races must repeat their seeded hash. It caught the sky-launch, the nondeterminism and the weapon balance without anyone looking at a picture.\\n- **Least helpful test:** the per-weapon \\\"fires once\\\" checks, which never failed. Menu screenshots were also low value beyond the glyph issues.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the fixed-step loop with `game.advance`, so whole races, the attract timer, replays, a stand-in hub and the split screen ran headless in seconds. Also the standard pause, settings, rebinding and boot screens, the chip synth with layers, and World3D taking plain three.js meshes with bloom.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. `E.World3D` doesn't exist when classic scripts run (the add-on is a deferred module), so `E.World3D.INPUT` crashed at boot. `game.advance` right after `game.go` doesn't switch scenes until a real frame passes. `audio.sfx` has no delay option, so the voice uses timers. The half-keyboard remap only covers the up/down/left/right actions, which forced me to move steering and pitch onto them.\\n- **Most important thing I built:** track-space hover physics on banked splines with crest air time and a gap jump, the mesh builders for track, tunnels, craft and scenery, the ten weapons and AI, and the 10-foot menu and glyph kit.\\n- **Hardest part:** using World3D as a pure renderer. It wants a level or terrain, so a one-tile pit level stands in. The engine axes (x east, y south, z up) map to three.js with a reflection, which made winding and camera-roll signs trial and error.\\n- **What I changed in the engine:** the button-symbol setting now defaults to PlayStation, sits under Display, and offers PlayStation or Xbox. It is marked `SNIPEOUT EDIT` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`.\\n- **One change I'd make:** make `E.World3D.INPUT` and `SETTINGS` available before the add-on loads, and add a levelless mode for custom-mesh worlds.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the plan's pinned versions, axis and unit conventions, determinism rules and hub skeleton. The one-command testing rule kept the build coherent.\\n- **Confusing:** the scale. Four tracks, six songs, split-screen VERSUS, replays, tunnels, gap jumps and eleven drills is more than one session builds. The plan also uses a different run-folder name than TASK.md (TASK.md won).\\n- **Hardest thing:** keeping every feature complete with no stubs while fitting the plan into one session.\\n- **What I'd change:** mark which plan features are mandatory and which may be cut, shorten the plan, and say whether a plan-driven build may drop plan-only features.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":656,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":397762,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":656},\"output_tokens\":9,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215\",\"uuid\":\"4ee70197-5fa7-4046-9d57-c01faa86f867\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:34:28.406Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh79FKsuDjWHYTMMHZGy\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML exists in the root, exit-interview.json parses with all fields answered, the four sections are present, and the suite passes. But the transcript never verifies every TASK.md feature against the build: the coverage table is asserted, and the final message contradicts itself about tunnels and scenery. The completeness requirement is not clearly demonstrated, and the earlier 'trim' and 'simpler scenery' wording was never fully withdrawn in the transcript.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215\",\"uuid\":\"d50d409d-92ce-4252-a38d-f35278ef919f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:34:29.601Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}"]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185013__xe162c9/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183420__xf7f2